    "teach_2": {
      "id": "teach_2",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Expressions can carry three kinds of brackets:\n\n( ) parentheses — the smallest\n{ } braces — the middle\n[ ] square brackets — the largest\n\nThey nest like boxes inside boxes:\n\n4 + [10 − {6 − (3 − 1)}]",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_2_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_2_step": {
      "id": "teach_2_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Open the innermost box first, and work outward:\n\n(3 − 1) = 2\n{6 − 2} = 4\n[10 − 4] = 6\n4 + 6 = 10\n\nOne layer per line. Each line removes exactly one pair of brackets.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_2"
        }
      ]
    },
