    "teach_4": {
      "id": "teach_4",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Some book expressions carry a small line drawn over part of them, like 9 + 6 with a bar on top.\n\nThat bar is called a virnaculum. It behaves exactly like a bracket — an invisible package.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_4_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_4_step": {
      "id": "teach_4_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "So in 25 − 9 + 6 with the bar over 9 + 6:\n\nfirst: 9 + 6 = 15\nthen: 25 − 15 = 10\n\nWithout the bar, left to right gives 25 − 9 + 6 = 22.\n\nRule: simplify whatever is under the bar before BODMAS even starts.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_4"
        }
      ]
    },
